From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:33:36 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ps1-cases

PlayStation games stand on the shelf as jewel cases faced with the front
cover (Labels/PS1/<stem>.png, ScreenScraper box-2D), fitted whole in a
square well on the colour of its own edge. The four cases are generated
neutrals coloured with the same Overlay as the retro carts: US and EU
(the same mould), Japanese with the spine strip over the cover's left
edge, and a double case for a playlist of two or more discs. The region
comes from the file name tags, then the SYSTEM.CNF serial. A game with
no cover gets a plain case with its title.

On insert the case opens and the disc slides into the slot along the
upstream insert path; the disc is faced with its label scan
(Labels/PS1/disc/<stem>.png, support-2D) or printed in the title colour.
